
TIME-SPAN WAIT EVALUATION — This is a time-spanning wait/stakeout action.
Your job is to determine what checks apply during the wait period.

- STEALTH: If the character is hiding while waiting, request a Stealth check. DC depends on the
  environment (urban alley with cover = DC 10-15, open field = DC 20+, crowd = DC 12).
- PERCEPTION: Request at least one Perception check for awareness during the wait. If the wait is
  long (4+ hours), request one per significant time block. DC depends on what they're watching for
  (obvious event = DC 10, subtle activity = DC 15+, hidden movement = DC 20+).
- FATIGUE: If the character has been awake 16+ hours by the end of the wait, they become fatigued.
  Request a Constitution check DC 10 if near the threshold.
- EXPOSURE: If waiting outdoors in harsh weather, Fortitude saves may be needed as per weather rules.
- DURATION ESTIMATE: Estimate how long the waited-for event takes based on narrative context.
  Set estimated_hours in wait_parameters.

Include all checks in player_rolls.
